  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "What is the cardinality of $K\\times K$ for $K={k,l,m,n,o,p,r,s}?$",
  "worked_solution": "For any two finite sets $A$ and $B,$ the cardinality of $A\\times B$ is\n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|K\\times K| & =|K|\\cdot |K| \\\\  & =8\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
